From 4a9fcb33eed2364d3caae5cb3c63c200069555a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:34:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AmgX nodal blocks: remarks of the review

- the conjugate gradient of AmgX uses the euclidean norm of the whole
  residual (use_scalar_norm): with blocks, AmgX checked the norm of each
  component separately;
- the positions of the block columns used by the conversion to blocks are
  proportional to the local size (array for the columns of the process,
  map for the other ones), and duplicated entries are summed;
- the matrices given by blocks must be square, with the same distribution
  of their rows and columns (checked by all the processes);
- tests: one application of the block Jacobi smoother of AmgX on the nodal
  blocks is the one of NodalBlockJacobi (one process: on several
  processes, the smoothers of AmgX 2.5 used alone give wrong results with
  blocks, documented), it differs on the scalar entries; the conjugate
  gradient of MFEM preconditioned by the aggregation multigrid with nodal
  blocks; single precision with blocks; parallel matrices on one process
  (AmgXSolverTestP1-gpu); invalid value of the option;
- documentation: iterations of the conjugate gradient of MFEM, coarsest
  level smoothed twice, aggregates paired from the first entry of each
  block, smoothers used alone with blocks in parallel, norm of the
  convergence criteria of AmgX with blocks.
